# Maxelerator GTM Studio

A team of five AI agents on **BAND** writes a go-to-market playbook for every startup in the
Maxelerator incubator/accelerator. **FlexPrice** meters each section the agents produce
against the startup's prepaid credit wallet, so the program knows exactly what each
playbook cost and can grant or sell credits.

```
 Program manager / founder / mentor
          │  "@Maxel Strategist build the playbook for qubit-sense"
          ▼
 ┌──────────────────────── BAND room (hosted) ────────────────────────┐
 │  Maxel Strategist ──@mentions──▶ Market Analyst · Pricing Architect │
 │        ▲                         Messaging Writer · Launch Planner  │
 │        └──────── "SECTION SAVED" ◀──── (work in parallel)           │
 └───────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
             │ studio tools (same code in BAND and local mode)
             ▼
   GetStartupProfile · CheckCredits · StartPlaybook · SaveSection · FinalizePlaybook
             │                                   │
             ▼                                   ▼
   Store (local disk or S3)            FlexPrice: customer + wallet per startup,
   profiles, sections, playbook.md     one usage event per section (maxel.credits)
```

## What you get per startup

One Markdown playbook with eight sections: executive summary, market and ICP, positioning
and messaging, pricing and packaging (with a ready FlexPrice setup for the startup's own
product), channels and partnerships (AWS Marketplace only when it fits), sales play, 90-day
launch plan, and metrics/risks/open questions. Cost: 95 credits, including the pricing-model assignment (configurable).

## Do I need AWS?

No. BAND and FlexPrice are hosted services; the studio is six small processes (an API and
five agents) that run anywhere Docker runs. `deploy/aws/` is optional, for programs with
AWS credits. AWS Marketplace appears in playbooks as a **sales channel for startups**,
recommended only when their buyers hold AWS committed spend.

## Quick start (5 minutes, no keys)

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
make demo          # onboard an example startup, build a playbook with the stub LLM, print it
make test          # 37 tests
```

## Execution steps (go live)

| # | Step | Command / where | Done when |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Install | `pip install -e ".[band,llm]"` (Python 3.11+) or `docker compose build` | `maxel --help` works |
| 2 | Configure | `cp .env.example .env`; add `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `MAXEL_ADMIN_TOKEN` | `.env` filled |
| 3 | FlexPrice | Feature `maxel.credits` (SUM `credits`), plan "Maxelerator Cohort"; set `MAXEL_METER=flexprice` ([guide](docs/FLEXPRICE_SETUP.md)) | `maxel flexprice ping` shows in the Event Debugger |
| 4 | BAND | Create 5 remote agents at app.band.ai, put IDs/keys in `.env` ([guide](docs/BAND_SETUP.md)) | each agent logs `Connected to platform` |
| 5 | Dry run | `MAXEL_LLM=anthropic maxel onboard examples/startups/qubit-sense.json && maxel run qubit-sense` | a real playbook in `maxel show qubit-sense` |
| 6 | Deploy | `docker compose up -d --build` (or `deploy/aws`) | `GET /health` returns `ok` |
| 7 | Onboard cohort | `maxel cohort import cohort.csv` | every startup has a wallet |
| 8 | Run in BAND | Room with the 5 agents + mentors; post `maxel band kickoff <id>` | `PLAYBOOK COMPLETE` in the room |
| 9 | Review | Mentor reviews each playbook with the founder in week 1 | feedback captured |

## Local Qwen pricing model

A fine-tuned local model (Qwen via `mlx_lm.server`) assigns each startup a pricing model. The
studio validates its answer, retries once, falls back to rules, and turns the approved result
into FlexPrice objects in the startup's own account:

```bash
maxel pricing recommend qubit-sense        # MAXEL_PRICING_LLM=openai -> local Qwen
maxel pricing approve qubit-sense          # mentor sign-off
maxel pricing apply qubit-sense            # dry run; add --execute with the startup's key
maxel training pricing-seed --count 150    # JSONL for Qwen Studio
```

Full guide: [docs/QWEN_LOCAL_MODEL.md](docs/QWEN_LOCAL_MODEL.md).

## Two ways to run a playbook

| | BAND mode | Local mode |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Start | Post the kickoff message in a BAND room | `maxel run <id>` or `POST /startups/<id>/playbooks {"mode":"local"}` |
| Agents | Five agents in parallel, coordinating by @mention | One process plays each role in turn |
| Humans in the loop | Mentors and founders join the room and redirect agents | No |
| Audit trail | Every exchange kept by BAND | Logs only |
| Billing | Identical (same tools, same events) | Identical |

## API

`maxel serve` (port 8080). All routes except `/health` need `Authorization: Bearer $MAXEL_ADMIN_TOKEN`.

```bash
curl -X POST localhost:8080/startups -H "Authorization: Bearer $T" -d @examples/startups/foldwise-bio.json
curl localhost:8080/startups/foldwise-bio/credits -H "Authorization: Bearer $T"
curl -X POST localhost:8080/startups/foldwise-bio/playbooks -H "Authorization: Bearer $T" -d '{"mode":"local"}'
curl "localhost:8080/startups/foldwise-bio/playbooks/latest?format=md" -H "Authorization: Bearer $T"
```

## Repo map

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `config/studio.yaml` | Sections, owners, credit costs, agent names. Change the playbook here. |
| `prompts/` | House rules + one prompt per agent role |
| `templates/playbook.md.j2` | Final playbook layout |
| `src/maxel/tools.py` | The tools agents call; where billing happens |
| `src/maxel/band_runtime.py` | Connects each role to BAND (Anthropic adapter + custom tools) |
| `src/maxel/local_runner.py` | Same playbook without BAND |
| `src/maxel/pricing.py` | Pricing-model schema, validation, rules baseline, FlexPrice plan builder |
| `src/maxel/training.py` | Training data for the local Qwen model |
| `src/maxel/metering.py` | FlexPrice client, idempotent meter, offline ledger |
| `src/maxel/provisioning.py` | Onboarding: FlexPrice customer + credit wallet |
| `src/maxel/api.py`, `cli.py` | HTTP API (Starlette) and `maxel` CLI |
| `deploy/aws/` | Optional AWS CDK stack (ECS Fargate + S3) |
| `examples/` | Two deeptech startup profiles and a cohort CSV |

## Customising

- **Add a section:** append it to `config/studio.yaml` with an `owner` and `credits`; the
  owner's prompt picks up the assignment automatically.
- **Change prices:** edit `credits` per section and `default_credits_per_startup`.
- **Add a specialist:** add a role in `config/studio.yaml`, a prompt in `prompts/`, a BAND
  agent, and a service in `docker-compose.yml`.
